### Strategy 1: Standard Read-Through (@Cacheable)
### First call = cache miss (slow ~1s), second call = cache hit (fast)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/standard

### Strategy 2: Conditional Caching
### Cached when category != 'uncached' and result is not empty
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/conditional?category=electronics

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/conditional?category=uncached

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/conditional?category=nonexistent

### Strategy 3: Short-lived TTL (60s)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/short-lived

### Strategy 4: Cache Update / Write-Through (@CachePut)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/update
Content-Type: application/json

{"id": 1, "name": "Laptop Pro", "category": "electronics", "price": 1299.99}

### Strategy 5: Cache Eviction (@CacheEvict)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/clear

### Strategy 6: Combined Multi-Cache Action (@Caching)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/bulk-update
Content-Type: application/json

{"id": 2, "name": "Wireless Headphones", "category": "electronics", "price": 199.99}

### Pub/Sub: Publish a message (check app logs for subscriber output)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/messages/publish
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "Item #1 has been updated"}
